IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p3-appointments`

-- Tests for Part 3 (ss 8A to 17 and the Schedule).  Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion.

-- s 8A(2): the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may sit in any State Court.
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the holder may sit in any State Court and act as a judge of it with all the jurisdiction, power and privileges of such a judge` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the holder may sit in any State Court and act as a judge of it with all the jurisdiction, power and privileges of such a judge` Magistrate EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8A(3): during the period of the appointment (inside the period yes; outside it no; not a Presiding Judge: not decided).
#ASSERT `s 8A(3) the person may continue to sit in the General Division of the High Court, the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8A(3) the person may continue to sit in the General Division of the High Court, the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8A(3) the person may continue to sit in the General Division of the High Court, the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8A(4) and s 9(4): after the appointment ends, the person continues to sit in a case he or she heard.
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the person continues to sit as a judge of the State Court to give judgment or otherwise in the case` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the person continues to sit as a judge of the State Court to give judgment or otherwise in the case` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the person continues to sit as a judge of the State Court to give judgment or otherwise in the case` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(4) the person is to sit as a District Judge for the purpose of giving judgment or otherwise in the case` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(4) the person is to sit as a District Judge for the purpose of giving judgment or otherwise in the case` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(4) the person is to sit as a District Judge for the purpose of giving judgment or otherwise in the case` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 9(3): 7 years (boundary 6/7); s 9(3A): 5 years and the Chief Justice's opinion (boundary 4/5).
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` 7 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge` 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(3A) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge despite subsection (3)` 5 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(3A) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge despite subsection (3)` 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(3A) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a District Judge despite subsection (3)` 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(5) the person is ex officio a Magistrate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(5) the person is ex officio a Magistrate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 10(2): 3 years (boundary 2/3); s 10(3): one year and the Chief Justice's opinion (boundary 0/1).
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate` 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate despite subsection (2)` 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate despite subsection (2)` 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the person may be appointed to be or to act as a Magistrate despite subsection (2)` 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 11(2) Justices of the Peace; s 12(2) registrar qualification; s 12(3), s 13.
#ASSERT `s 11(2) Justices of the Peace have and may exercise the power or perform the duty of a Magistrate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(2) Justices of the Peace have and may exercise the power or perform the duty of a Magistrate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the holder is ex officio a commissioner for oaths` `Registrar of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the holder is ex officio a commissioner for oaths` `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the holder is ex officio a commissioner for oaths` Magistrate EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13 the holder may exercise the powers and duties conferred and imposed on the registrar` `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 the holder may exercise the powers and duties conferred and imposed on the registrar` `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13 the holder may exercise the powers and duties conferred and imposed on the registrar` Bailiff FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 15(1): bailiffs and process servers have the three duties.
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` Bailiff `Execute the writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and other mandatory processes of the State Courts given to them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` `Process server` `Make a return of the same, with the manner of the execution, to the court from which the process issued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` Bailiff `Arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` Bailiff `Some other duty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the holder is to do the duty` Interpreter `Arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 15(2), s 15A.
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the registrar may engage the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the registrar may engage the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the registrar may engage the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15A(1) the registrar may authorise the person to exercise the powers and perform the duties of a bailiff` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15A(1) the registrar may authorise the person to exercise the powers and perform the duties of a bailiff` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15A(1) the registrar may authorise the person to exercise the powers and perform the duties of a bailiff` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15A(2) section 68(2) applies to the person as it applies to an officer of a State Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15A(2) section 68(2) applies to the person as it applies to an officer of a State Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 16: entry while executing an enforcement order; breaking open only if necessary, with no more force than reasonably necessary.
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may effect an entry into a building` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may effect an entry into a building` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may effect an entry into a building` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may break open an outer or inner door or window of the building or any receptacle in it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may break open an outer or inner door or window of the building or any receptacle in it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16 the bailiff may break open an outer or inner door or window of the building or any receptacle in it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 17(1): judicial officers, and other officers the Chief Justice requires, take the oath first.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions of the office` `District Judge` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions of the office` `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions of the office` Bailiff TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions of the office` Bailiff FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the oath was taken and subscribed before the functions of the office were exercised as the section requires` `District Judge` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the oath was taken and subscribed before the functions of the office were exercised as the section requires` `District Judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The Schedule: three oaths, and which one section 17(1) requires of whom.
#ASSERT `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`'s `item of the Schedule` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Schedule para 2 the oath of office of an interpreter`'s `item of the Schedule` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`'s `item of the Schedule` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Schedule the oath that section 17(1) requires of the holder` Magistrate EQUALS JUST `Schedule para 1 the oath of office and allegiance of a judicial officer`
#ASSERT `Schedule the oath that section 17(1) requires of the holder` Interpreter EQUALS JUST `Schedule para 2 the oath of office of an interpreter`
#ASSERT `Schedule the oath that section 17(1) requires of the holder` Bailiff EQUALS JUST `Schedule para 3 the oath of office of other officer of a court`
#ASSERT `Schedule the oath that section 17(1) requires of the holder` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 17(2), (2A), (3), (4).
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the oath may be taken and subscribed before the person` `The Presiding Judge of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the oath may be taken and subscribed before the person` `The Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the oath may be taken and subscribed before the person` `A Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) the oath may be taken and subscribed before the person` `Someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(2A) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing through a live video link or live television link` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(3) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted a certified copy as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(3) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted a certified copy as the section requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(3) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted a certified copy as the section requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(3) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted a certified copy as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(4) the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted the certified copies as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(4) the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted the certified copies as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(4) the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts has entered the oath in the record and transmitted the certified copies as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rules, run with #TRACE (read, not asserted): the bailiffs' duties of s 15(1) and the oath of s 17(1).
#TRACE `s 15(1)(a) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to execute the processes given to them` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server` DOES `execute a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process` AT 4
#TRACE `s 15(1)(b) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to make a return of the execution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server` DOES `make a return of the process and the manner of its execution to the court from which it issued` AT 6
#TRACE `s 15(1)(c) duty: bailiffs and process servers are to arrest and receive the persons and property committed to custody` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A bailiff or process server` DOES `arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts` AT 6
#TRACE `s 17(1) duty: a judicial officer is to take and subscribe the oath before exercising the functions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A judicial officer` DOES `take and subscribe the oath of office` AT 1
